  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Lucas Delgado, Santa Úrsula, Tenerife, a villa on a 4,200 m2 cliff plot): from the sea a stack of three white horizontal slabs, each stepping in over the one below, with glass balustrades along the terrace edges and a small glass-and-white box on top; the lowest level is a basalt stone wall with glazing; a long timber deck round an infinity pool that dissolves into the sea (photographs 1 and 3); at the road a low concrete entrance pavilion - a wedge of concrete lintel over a timber pivot door - behind a fence of timber and a row of royal palms; inside a curling white spiral stair round an olive tree in a courtyard with water. Materials per the article: basalt stone, concrete and wood. Modelled: the three slabs and top box, basalt base, deck and pool, balustrades, the entrance pavilion and palms, the lava-slope ground (rubble), the sea strip at the south. Guessed: dimensions (a 28 x 14 m footprint), the plot's shape, side walls. A private home placed at its town only (Santa Úrsula)."
